<title>THAILAND: Securities One reviewed Q3 net plunges.</title>
<headline>Securities One reviewed Q3 net plunges.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1996-11-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Reviewed, consolidated financial</p>
<p>results for the period ending Septemer 30, 1996.</p>
<p>		   (in millions of baht unless stated)</p>
<p>			     Third quarter</p>
<p>				   1996			1995</p>
<p>    Share (baht)	     1.11     vs	     2.73</p>
<p>    Net			104.98     vs	   245.72</p>
<p>				Nine months</p>
<p>    Share (baht)	     6.99     vs	     9.21</p>
<p>    Net			642.10     vs	   829.26</p>
<p>NOTE - Securities One Plc, a finance firm, said the sharp decline in profits in the period was due to a drop in securities trading on the Stock Exchange of Thailand. This decline in trading caused the company's brokerage fees and other fees to drop by 28 percent.</p>
<p>Previously Securities One announced unaudited results for the third quarter of 109.95 million baht or 0.93 a share vs 181.77 million baht or 2.02 a share. For the nine-month period its unreviewed earnings amounted to 626.23 million baht or 5.32 per share vs 726.6 million baht or 8.07 per share.</p>
<p>-- Bangkok newsroom (662) 652-0642</p>
</text>
